<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Helios Cloud Power Forecasting</title>
<meta name="description" content="Probabilistic data-center power forecasting, CPU vs GPU benchmarks and carbon-aware scheduling for the fictional cloud operator Helios Cloud.">
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #f7f7f4; --surface: #ffffff; --ink: #0b0b0b; --ink-2: #52514e; --muted: #898781;
    --line: #e1e0d9; --accent: #2a78d6; --good: #1b8a5a; --chip: #eef3fb;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
         font: 15px/1.55 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; }
  header.hero { background: var(--surface); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .wrap { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 16px; }
  .hero .wrap { padding-top: 28px; padding-bottom: 18px; }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 12px; }
  h1 { font-size: 28px; line-height: 1.2; margin: 6px 0 8px; }
  h2 { font-size: 21px; margin: 0 0 6px; }
  h3 { font-size: 16px; margin: 18px 0 6px; }
  p.lead { color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 860px; margin: 0; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; margin-top: 10px; }
  nav.toc { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 5; background: rgba(255,255,255,.96);
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  nav.toc .wrap { display: flex; gap: 18px; overflow-x: auto; padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 10px; }
  nav.toc a { color: var(--ink-2); text-decoration: none; font-size: 14px; white-space: nowrap; }
  nav.toc a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  section { padding: 26px 0 8px; }
  .card { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px;
          padding: 16px; margin: 12px 0; overflow-x: auto; }
  .kpis { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .kpi { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; }
  .kpi .label { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 13px; }
  .kpi .value { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 650; margin: 2px 0; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .kpi .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.5px; }
  .grid2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(420px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  table.tbl { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 13px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  table.tbl th { text-align: right; color: var(--ink-2); font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
                 padding: 6px 8px; white-space: nowrap; }
  table.tbl td { text-align: right; padding: 5px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f0efe9; white-space: nowrap; }
  table.tbl th:first-child, table.tbl td:first-child { text-align: left; }
  table.tbl tr:hover td { background: #fafaf7; }
  .chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin: 8px 0; }
  .chip { background: var(--chip); color: #184f95; border-radius: 999px; padding: 3px 10px; font-size: 12.5px; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  ul.tight { margin: 6px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  footer { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; padding: 30px 0 40px; }
  code { background: #f0efe9; padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 13px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .grid2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } h1 { font-size: 23px; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Helios Cloud &middot; fictional operator &middot; dcforecast {{ version }}</div>
    <h1>Data-center power forecasting and carbon-aware scheduling</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Probabilistic 24-hour-ahead forecasts (P10 / P50 / P90) of facility power for {{ n_sites }} sites,
      trained on a laptop GPU and turned into energy, cost and carbon decisions. All data is synthetic
      and generated by a documented, physically-motivated model; every number below comes from a real
      pipeline run.
    </p>
    <div class="meta">Profile <code>{{ profile }}</code> &middot; history {{ start }} to {{ end }} &middot;
      {{ "{:,}".format(n_rows) }} site-hours &middot; generated {{ generated }}</div>
    {% if kpis %}
    <div class="kpis">
      {% for k in kpis %}
      <div class="kpi"><div class="label">{{ k.label }}</div><div class="value">{{ k.value }}</div><div class="note">{{ k.note }}</div></div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</header>
<nav class="toc"><div class="wrap">
  <a href="#data">Data</a>
  {% if leaderboard_table %}<a href="#forecast">Forecasts</a><a href="#leaderboard">Leaderboard</a>{% endif %}
  {% if bench_table %}<a href="#benchmark">CPU vs GPU</a>{% endif %}
  {% if decision %}<a href="#decision">Decisions</a>{% endif %}
  <a href="#method">Method</a>
</div></nav>

<main class="wrap">
<section id="data">
  <h2>1. Telemetry and data quality</h2>
  <p class="muted">Hourly facility power = IT load x PUE, where PUE rises with outside temperature once a site
    leaves its free-cooling regime. Sensor faults (gaps, spikes, stuck values) are injected and then detected and
    imputed by the cleaning step.</p>
  <div class="card">{{ fig_overview|safe }}</div>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card"><h3>Sites</h3>{{ sites_table|safe }}</div>
    <div class="card"><h3>QA report (cleaning step)</h3>
      <div class="chips">
        <span class="chip">rows received {{ "{:,}".format(qa.totals.rows_received) }} / {{ "{:,}".format(qa.totals.rows_expected) }}</span>
        <span class="chip">spike recall {{ "%.1f"|format(qa.detection.spike_recall * 100) }}%</span>
        <span class="chip">stuck recall {{ "%.1f"|format(qa.detection.stuck_recall * 100) }}%</span>
        <span class="chip">flag precision {{ "%.1f"|format(qa.detection.precision * 100) }}%</span>
        <span class="chip">facility imputed {{ "%.2f"|format(qa.facility_imputed_pct) }}%</span>
        <span class="chip">imputation MAPE {{ "%.2f"|format(qa.imputation_error.facility_kw.mape_pct) }}%</span>
      </div>
      {{ qa_table|safe }}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% if leaderboard_table %}
<section id="forecast">
  <h2>2. Forecast vs actual</h2>
  <p class="muted">Production model <b>{{ prod_model }}</b> ({{ prod_reason }}) on the last backtest fold: daily
    24-hour-ahead forecasts issued at 00:00 UTC with a P10-P90 band.</p>
  <div class="card">{{ fig_forecast|safe }}</div>
</section>

<section id="leaderboard">
  <h2>3. Rolling-origin backtest</h2>
  <p class="muted">{{ folds|length }} folds; each model is refit on all data before the fold and forecasts every day of
    the test window. MASE is scaled by the in-sample seasonal-naive (24 h) error; coverage is the share of actuals
    inside the P10-P90 band (target 80%).</p>
  <div class="chips">
    {% for f in folds %}<span class="chip">fold {{ f.fold }}: {{ f.test_start[:10] }} to {{ f.test_end[:10] }}</span>{% endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class="card">{{ leaderboard_table|safe }}</div>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card">{{ fig_leaderboard|safe }}</div>
    <div class="card">{{ fig_horizon|safe }}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card"><h3>MASE per site</h3>{{ site_table|safe }}</div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Backtest compute</h3>{{ timings_table|safe }}</div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

{% if bench_table %}
<section id="benchmark">
  <h2>4. CPU vs GPU training and inference</h2>
  <p class="muted">Same model and data; GPU at batch {{ bench_cfg.batch_size }} (what the VRAM-aware finder picks),
    CPU at its default training batch {{ bench_cfg.cpu_batch_size }}; measured on
    {{ hw.cpu_model }} ({{ hw.cpu_physical_cores }} cores) and
    {% if hw.gpus %}{{ hw.gpus[0].name }} ({{ hw.gpus[0].vram_total_gb }} GB, CUDA {{ hw.gpus[0].cuda_version }}){% else %}no CUDA GPU{% endif %},
    host anonymised as <code>{{ hw.host }}</code>. GPU utilisation is sampled with nvidia-smi during training;
    CPU% and RSS with psutil.</p>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card">{{ fig_bench_train|safe }}</div>
    <div class="card">{{ fig_bench_infer|safe }}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">{{ bench_table|safe }}</div>
</section>
{% endif %}

{% if decision %}
<section id="decision">
  <h2>5. From forecast to decisions</h2>
  <p class="muted">Next {{ decision.horizon_hours }} hours from {{ decision.origin[:16] }} UTC. The P50 forecast is
    converted into energy, cost and carbon per site; then {{ "%.0f"|format(decision.deferrable_mwh) }} MWh of
    deferrable batch compute is placed by a linear program under per-site power caps.</p>
  <div class="card"><h3>Expected energy, cost and carbon</h3>{{ rollup_table|safe }}
    {% if decision.forecast_vs_realized %}
    <p class="muted">Checked against the held-out future: forecast energy error
      {{ "%+.2f"|format(decision.forecast_vs_realized.energy_error_pct) }}%, hourly MAPE
      {{ "%.2f"|format(decision.forecast_vs_realized.hourly_mape_pct) }}%, P10-P90 coverage
      {{ "%.0f"|format(decision.forecast_vs_realized.p10_p90_coverage * 100) }}%.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="card"><h3>Scheduling plans vs running immediately</h3>{{ plans_table|safe }}</div>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card">{{ fig_ci|safe }}</div>
    <div class="card">{{ fig_plan|safe }}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">{{ fig_pareto|safe }}</div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section id="method">
  <h2>6. Method notes</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <ul class="tight">
      <li>Features are leakage-safe: every lag is at least 24 h old at forecast time and rolling statistics use only
        the past. Weather covariates assume a day-ahead weather forecast is available when the forecast is issued
        (the generator stores a noisy forecast next to the truth).</li>
      <li>Deep models are global (one network for all sites, with a site embedding) and forecast all 24 horizons at
        once with a pinball loss on P10 / P50 / P90.</li>
      <li>Training uses AMP on CUDA, pinned memory, gradient clipping, OneCycle LR, early stopping with
        checkpointing and a VRAM-aware batch-size finder that keeps well inside a shared 4 GB GPU.</li>
      <li>The scheduler is an LP (scipy HiGHS): move deferrable energy into low-carbon (or low-cost) hours and,
        for a portable share, to other sites, without exceeding facility power caps.</li>
    </ul>
    {% if timings %}
    <p class="muted">Pipeline wall-clock (s):
      {% for k, v in timings.items() %}{{ k }} {{ "%.0f"|format(v) }}{% if not loop.last %} &middot; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if resources %}
    <p class="muted">Footprint: peak process memory {{ "%.0f"|format(resources.peak_rss_mb or 0) }} MB
      {% if resources.gpu_peak_allocated_train_mb %}&middot; GPU peak allocated while training {{ "%.0f"|format(resources.gpu_peak_allocated_train_mb) }} MB{% endif %}
      &middot; on disk: data {{ "%.0f"|format(resources.disk_mb.data) }} MB, runs {{ "%.0f"|format(resources.disk_mb.runs) }} MB,
      reports {{ "%.0f"|format(resources.disk_mb.reports) }} MB.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>
</main>
<footer><div class="wrap">
  Helios Cloud is a fictional company; all data is synthetic. Built with dcforecast {{ version }} &middot;
  MIT licence &middot; Advaith A Arun.
</div></footer>
</body>
</html>
